# tools/polygon_witness.rish -- an ordered contour ring simplified to its defining VERTICES by Douglas-Peucker, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/contour.rye hands back a component's OUTER BOUNDARY as an ordered clockwise ring of
# pixel coordinates, one point per boundary pixel: a 5x5 block traces to a 16-point ring. That ring names a shape by every pixel
# on its edge rather than by the CORNERS a human eye reads. This rung reads that missing fact -- the minimal ordered set of
# VERTICES whose straight edges reproduce the ring within a tolerance, so a dozen boundary pixels become the four points that
# draw the shape.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a solid 5x5 block's 16-pixel ring reduces at tolerance 0.5 to EXACTLY the four corner
# vertices, a fact the raw ring's sixteen pixels cannot name; the polygon is an ordered subset of the ring inventing no point; a
# spread 2x8 strip likewise reduces to four corners (a straight run collapses to its endpoints regardless of length); the
# CORNER-COUNT contrast -- an L-shape at the SAME tolerance reduces to MORE THAN FOUR vertices where the rectangle reduced to
# four, the polygon reading each shape's real corner count no area, box, center, moment, or ring length can give; the tolerance
# knob coarsens monotonically down to the two-vertex floor a closed ring can never fall below; refusals by name. No network, no
# key, no funds -- the vertices a surface names the day it draws or matches a shape by its corners, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/polygon_witness.rish

say "polygon: Language EN -- Season G Douglas-Peucker polygon simplifier over a Contour ring; simplify reduces the ordered ring to its defining vertices, a corner detector and a vector outline read from it."
say "polygon: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the vertex-selection choice (the farthest-point anchor split, the perpendicular distance, the keep-or-drop decision); contour owns the ordered ring and its Point type. No gather, no blend, no codec, no color, not even a pixel-writing loop -- a polygon is a reading, not a render."
say "polygon: Lens TAME -- the kept-vertex set and the Douglas-Peucker work stack are both sized to the ring length (bounded by the pixel ceiling); the stack guards PolygonTooComplex by name; an empty ring refuses EmptyContour and a negative tolerance refuses BadTolerance up front so a refusal allocates nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/polygon"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/polygon.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "polygon: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "polygon: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "polygon: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-polygon" else "polygon: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "polygon: GREEN -- the 5x5 block's 16-pixel ring reduces to exactly its four corner vertices, the polygon is an ordered subset of the ring, a spread 2x8 strip reduces to four corners, an L reduces to more than four at the same tolerance (the corner-count contrast), the tolerance knob coarsens to the two-vertex floor, the refusals fire by name, on metal."
